{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\Asus\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\urdu-dua-ruqyah\\\\references\\\\project-scope.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Complete project scope\n\nWorkspace: `G:\\dua-ruqyah\\dua_main_ur_translation`\n\nDatabases: `G:\\dua-ruqyah\\dua_main_en.sqlite` and `G:\\dua-ruqyah\\dua_main_bn.sqlite`.\n\nUse English where it represents the same dataset and gives clearer translation context. Use Bengali where the English database has different/missing rows. Bengali remains a cross-check for English-sourced tables.\n\n| Table | Required source | Key | Translate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `categories` | EN, check BN | `id` | `name` |\n| `subcategories` | EN, check BN | `id` | `name` |\n| `dua_infos` | BN | `id` | `name`, `description` |\n| `duas` | EN, check BN | `id` | `name`, `content`, `translation`, `note`, plus text inside `groups` |\n| `ruqyah_categories` | EN, check BN | `id` | `name` |\n| `ruqyah_details` | EN | `id` | `topic_name`, `text` |\n| `ruqyah_instants` | EN, check BN | `id` | `topic_name`, `name`, `content`, `translation` |\n| `sections` | EN | `id`, `book_id` | `name` |\n| `ruqyah_subcategories` | EN, check BN | `id` | `name` |\n| `books` | BN | `id` | `name`, `writer`, `translator`, `editor` |\n| `book_details` | BN | `id`, `book_id`, `section_id` | `topic_name`, `description` |\n| `ruqyah_videos` | BN | `id` | `name`, `author` |\n| `drawer_items` | BN | `id` | `title`, `hero_title1`, `hero_title2`, and all human text inside `content` JSON |\n| `ids` | BN | `current_id` | no text; preserve and verify |\n| `drawer_item_actions` | structural base | `id` | translate `label`/human `action_data` if rows ever exist; currently preserve and verify |\n\nThe source choice determines both row identity and frozen values. The final database should use the fuller English schema while replacing each BN-routed table wholesale before Urdu target values are applied.\n\n## Known current scope defect\n\nThe existing `metadata/chunk_index.json` omits `sections`, `books`, `book_details`, and `drawer_items`. Existing progress therefore cannot represent whole-database completion. Add those tables without deleting or regenerating the existing translated chunks.\n\nThe current `scripts/generate.py` also has exclusions that conflict with complete scope. Do not run it until it has been made migration-safe and those exclusions have been removed.\n\n## Status meanings\n\n- `missing_scope`: required table absent from the chunk index.\n- `pending`: no target text filled.\n- `in_progress`: some target text filled.\n- `translated`: all target slots filled, but review evidence is incomplete.\n- `verified`: structural verifier passed.\n- `reviewed`: verified and separately reviewed for natural Urdu and accuracy.\n- `complete`: every required table reviewed and final database validation passed.\n\nDo not collapse `translated`, `verified`, and `reviewed` into the same claim.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\Asus\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\urdu-dua-ruqyah\\\\references\\\\urdu-style.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Natural Urdu standard\n\nWrite contemporary, educated Pakistani Urdu suitable for worship, guidance, and general app screens. It should sound authored in Urdu, not converted sentence by sentence from English or Bengali.\n\n## Voice\n\n- Use calm, respectful, devotional language without artificial grandeur.\n- Prefer familiar, flowing Urdu sentence order. Break unwieldy source sentences where meaning and markup permit.\n- Address the reader consistently and respectfully; avoid casual `├ÿ┬¬├ÖΓÇª` unless a quoted source requires it.\n- Use idiomatic verbs and complete predicates. Avoid noun-heavy calques and English-style passive chains.\n- Use common Urdu vocabulary where it is precise. Retain established Islamic Arabic terms rather than replacing them with Hindi/Sanskrit or awkward explanatory phrases.\n- Do not add sermons, rulings, praise, or explanations absent from the source.\n\n## Religious wording\n\n- Use `├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇ₧├ÖΓÇ₧├¢┬ü` consistently, not variant spellings.\n- Use `├ÿ┬»├ÿ┬╣├ÿ┬º`, `├ÿ┬░├Ü┬⌐├ÿ┬▒`, `├ÿ┬º├ÿ┬░├Ü┬⌐├ÿ┬º├ÿ┬▒`, `├ÖΓÇá├ÖΓÇª├ÿ┬º├ÿ┬▓`, `├ÿ┬▒├Ü┬⌐├Ö╦å├ÿ┬╣`, `├ÿ┬│├ÿ┬¼├ÿ┬»├¢┬ü`, `├ÿ┬¬├Ö╦å├ÿ┬¿├¢┬ü`, `├ÿ┬º├ÿ┬│├ÿ┬¬├ÿ┬║├Ö┬ü├ÿ┬º├ÿ┬▒`, `├ÿ┬▒├ÖΓÇÜ├¢┼Æ├¢┬ü` according to the glossary.\n- Preserve established honorifics accurately: `├ÿ┬▒├ÿ┬│├Ö╦å├ÖΓÇ₧ ├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇ₧├ÖΓÇ₧├¢┬ü ├»┬╖┬║`, `├ÿ┬▒├ÿ┬╢├¢┼Æ ├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇ₧├ÖΓÇ₧├¢┬ü ├ÿ┬╣├ÖΓÇá├¢┬ü/├ÿ┬╣├ÖΓÇá├¢┬ü├ÿ┬º/├ÿ┬╣├ÖΓÇá├¢┬ü├ÖΓÇª├ÿ┬º`, `├ÿ┬▒├ÿ┬¡├ÖΓÇª├¢┬ü ├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇ₧├ÖΓÇ₧├¢┬ü`, and `├ÿ┬╣├ÖΓÇ₧├¢┼Æ├¢┬ü ├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇ₧├ÿ┬│├ÖΓÇ₧├ÿ┬º├ÖΓÇª`. Attach them only to the correct person.\n- Use established Urdu spellings for prophets, Companions, scholars, surahs, collections, and places. Keep one spelling throughout.\n- Translate the meaning of Quran/hadith prose faithfully while leaving Arabic fields and Arabic blocks untouched.\n\n## Human-quality rejection signs\n\nRewrite text that has any of these traits:\n\n- source-language word order, repeated pronouns, or stiff literal connectors;\n- unnecessary English words when natural Urdu exists;\n- Bengali script or Bengali grammatical structure;\n- mixed respectful and casual address;\n- incorrect gender, number, agreement, postpositions, or compound verbs;\n- excessive Persianized formality that obscures a simple source;\n- machine-like repetition, fragmented clauses, or untranslated labels;\n- a title that names a different action/person/time from its content;\n- numbers interpreted as dates, ages, or quantities not present in the source.\n\n## Review aloud\n\nAfter semantic comparison, read each target as continuous Urdu without looking at the source. It must be immediately understandable, grammatically complete, and natural when spoken. Then compare again with the source to ensure fluency did not remove qualifications, negation, speakers, references, or repetitions.\n\nKeep ASCII digits in references and technical identifiers. Keep inline citations in normalized English unless the project glossary explicitly defines a different approved presentation.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
